axiom_published	allocator invariant	none (assumption)
# Ghost permissions to the two init-once atomics; their wrappers are the only accesses.
LinePerm	atomics primitive	loom/GenMC
StatePerm	atomics primitive	loom/GenMC
# The init-once protocol: what STATE's and the statics' invariants hold.
axiom_ready	allocator invariant	none (assumption)
axiom_state	allocator invariant	none (assumption)
axiom_statics	allocator invariant	none (assumption)
# Passes function pointers, which Verus does not support.
pthread_atfork_handlers	function pointer	none (assumption)
# The fork handler handoff: glibc runs the parent and child handlers on the
# thread whose prepare handler returned holding the locks and the mask.
# The handlers call axiom_fork_resumed_state only when FORK_LOCKED (verified
# atomics) says this fork's prepare took the locks: glibc serialises one
# fork's handlers under its atfork lock, so the flag read is this fork's.
axiom_fork_resumed_state	platform/kernel fact	none (assumption)
axiom_fork_resumed_sig	platform/kernel fact	none (assumption)
axiom_fork_resumed	platform/kernel fact	none (assumption)
# The fork child's orphaned feature line: only the forking thread runs there.
axiom_line_orphaned	allocator invariant	none (assumption)
# Raw-pointer projections of the init-once statics: each returns one pointer,
# its static's storage, and `shared_ptr` and `shared_storage_ptr` agree.
shared_ptr	UnsafeCell/volatile/transmute	Kani	trusted (partly checked, Kani: api::kani_statics::shared_ptrs_agree; not checked: that it carries the provenance of `shared_storage_ptr`'s pointer, which it derives another way (the harness compares addresses))	contract 1380591404, body 29835824
shared_storage_ptr	UnsafeCell/volatile/transmute	Kani	discharged (Kani: api::kani_statics::shared_ptrs_agree)	contract 2098755632, body 507721659
features_ptr	UnsafeCell/volatile/transmute	Kani	discharged (Kani: api::kani_statics::feature_ptrs_fixed)	contract 2881023278, body 531095909
line_ptr	UnsafeCell/volatile/transmute	Kani	discharged (Kani: api::kani_statics::feature_ptrs_fixed)	contract 2262815526, body 756715309
# Empty-template register hint: verus/emptyasm/run.sh checks the block adds
# no instruction to the shipped code (a verus/emptyasm/blocks.txt row).
shared_base	inline asm	Islaris/Isla	trusted (partly checked, emptyasm: shared_base in src/api/mod.rs; not checked: that `shared_ptr` returns that pointer (itself trusted, its address checked by a Kani harness), and the pointer's provenance; the check shows only that the asm! block emits no instruction)	contract 534596380, body 2091081502
# loom and C11 (verus/WEAKMEM.md, P4): `STATE` has two writes,
# `state_claim`'s exchange and `state_publish`'s `READY` store
# (tests/loom/tests/access.rs), so its modification order is `UNINIT`,
# `INITIALISING`, `READY`, each written once, and the permission's value
# reads as the last of them. C++20's exchange is a read-modify-write,
# which reads the last value for every ordering ([atomics.order] p10), in
# the strong form, which fails only when the value differs; a load reads a
# write no older than the last one that happens before it (coherence,
# [intro.races]); the `Release` store of `READY` with an `Acquire` load or
# exchange that reads it orders `init`'s plain writes before the reader (a
# release/acquire pair, [atomics.order] p2). The init models check this on
# a copy of `init_slow`, `shared` and `shared_if_ready` (`STATE`,
# `INIT_TID` and `SHARED` are statics built in `const` context, which loom
# cannot construct).
state_load	atomics primitive	loom/GenMC	trusted (partly checked, loom: init::loom_init_free_races_init, init::loom_init_two_callers, init::loom_init_reentry_aborts and init::loom_init_publisher_reads_ready; not checked: this body, which the models replace with loom's `load` inside a copy of the init steps, with the callers tests/loom/src/init.rs states; the C11 argument above that the permission's value is `STATE`'s last write, which tests/loom/tests/access.rs backs by matching source text only)	contract 3749283829, body 2433046193
state_claim	atomics primitive	loom/GenMC	trusted (partly checked, loom: init::loom_init_free_races_init, init::loom_init_two_callers and init::loom_init_reentry_aborts; not checked: this body, which the models replace with loom's `compare_exchange` inside a copy of the init steps, with the callers tests/loom/src/init.rs states; that it never fails spuriously, which loom's compare-and-swap cannot show and rests on `core`'s documentation of the strong form; the C11 argument above, which tests/loom/tests/access.rs backs by matching source text only)	contract 85710167, body 4074283701
state_publish	atomics primitive	loom/GenMC	trusted (partly checked, loom: init::loom_init_free_races_init, init::loom_init_two_callers, init::loom_init_reentry_aborts and init::loom_init_publisher_reads_ready; not checked: this body, which the models replace with loom's `store` inside a copy of the init steps, with the callers tests/loom/src/init.rs states (the readback after the store is a load the model adds); the C11 argument above, which tests/loom/tests/access.rs backs by matching source text only)	contract 2256376580, body 4059210318
# The same for the feature line: `LINE_STATE` has two writes outside the
# tests, `line_compare_exchange`'s and `line_store`'s, and no other file
# names it (tests/loom/tests/access.rs); the `Release` store of
# `LINE_READY` with an `Acquire` load or exchange publishes the line the
# builder wrote. The oncecell models check that hand-off and the fork
# child's reset on a copy of the line steps.
line_load	atomics primitive	loom/GenMC	trusted (partly checked, loom: oncecell::loom_oncecell_line_two_requests and oncecell::loom_oncecell_line_fork_child_rebuilds; not checked: this body, which the models replace with loom's `load` inside a copy of the line steps, with the requests tests/loom/src/oncecell.rs states; the C11 argument above that the permission's value is `LINE_STATE`'s last write, which tests/loom/tests/access.rs backs by matching source text only)	contract 2771109588, body 2110027002
line_compare_exchange	atomics primitive	loom/GenMC	trusted (partly checked, loom: oncecell::loom_oncecell_line_two_requests and oncecell::loom_oncecell_line_fork_child_rebuilds; not checked: this body, which the models replace with loom's `compare_exchange` inside a copy of the line steps, with the requests tests/loom/src/oncecell.rs states; that it never fails spuriously, which loom's compare-and-swap cannot show and rests on `core`'s documentation of the strong form; the C11 argument above, which tests/loom/tests/access.rs backs by matching source text only)	contract 1382960686, body 856950910
line_store	atomics primitive	loom/GenMC	trusted (partly checked, loom: oncecell::loom_oncecell_line_two_requests and oncecell::loom_oncecell_line_fork_child_rebuilds; not checked: this body, which the models replace with loom's `store` inside a copy of the line steps, with the requests tests/loom/src/oncecell.rs states; the C11 argument above, which tests/loom/tests/access.rs backs by matching source text only)	contract 3106292439, body 2809660891
# Termination of `init_slow`'s wait, given that `init` returns, a fair
# scheduler and that a store becomes visible in finite time (C++20
# [intro.progress] says it should): a waiter read `INITIALISING`, which
# only the one successful exchange writes, and that thread stores `READY`
# after `init`; were the waiter that thread, its `INIT_TID` load would
# read its own tid (read-after-write coherence) and it would abort. The
# init models check that no waiter is left spinning and that only the
# initialising thread takes the re-entry abort, on a copy.
init_slow	termination	loom/GenMC	trusted (partly checked, loom: init::loom_init_free_races_init, init::loom_init_two_callers and init::loom_init_reentry_aborts; not checked: this body, which the models replace with a copy, with the callers tests/loom/src/init.rs states and one waiter at a time; termination itself, which rests on `init` returning, a fair scheduler and visible stores, as loom models them; a child forked while `init` runs, or a signal handler on the initialising thread that allocates before its `INIT_TID` store, spins for ever, outside the C contract)	contract 1867649379, body 4001748639
